---
/*
 * /compare/ - the index for the comparison pages.
 *
 * Cards are generated from COMPARISONS. Nothing is hardcoded here, so adding a
 * comparison to the data file adds it to this page and to the sitemap.
 * No prices for any product, on this page or on the ones it links to.
 */
import Base from '~/layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '~/data/site';
import { COMPARISONS } from '~/data/comparisons';
import type { Comparison } from '~/data/comparisons';

const text = (v: unknown): string => (typeof v === 'string' ? v.trim() : '');

const items: Comparison[] = (Array.isArray(COMPARISONS) ? COMPARISONS : []).filter(
  (c) => c && text(c.slug).length > 0 && text(c.product).length > 0,
);

const pageUrl = `${SITE.url}/compare/`;

const schema: object[] = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: SITE.url },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Compare', item: pageUrl },
    ],
  },
];

if (items.length > 0) {
  schema.push({
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'ItemList',
    name: 'Odoo compared with the alternatives',
    url: pageUrl,
    numberOfItems: items.length,
    itemListElement: items.map((c, idx) => ({
      '@type': 'ListItem',
      position: idx + 1,
      name: `Odoo vs ${text(c.product)}`,
      url: `${SITE.url}/compare/${text(c.slug)}/`,
    })),
  });
}
---
<Base
  title="Odoo compared with the alternatives"
  description="Honest comparisons of Odoo against SAP, NetSuite, Business Central, Zoho, QuickBooks, Sage, Tally, SAP Business One, ERPNext and spreadsheets. Structural facts, no pricing, and the cases where the other product wins."
  structuredData={schema}
>
  <section class="bg-ink-900 text-white">
    <div class="container-site py-16 sm:py-24">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <div class="eyebrow text-brand-300">Compare</div>
        <h1 class="h1 mt-4">Odoo, compared with what you are actually considering.</h1>
        <p class="lede mt-6 text-ink-300">
          {items.length > 0
            ? `${items.length} comparisons written the way we would explain them on a call: structural facts, and the cases where the other product is the better choice.`
            : 'Comparisons written the way we would explain them on a call: structural facts, and the cases where the other product is the better choice.'}
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section pb-0">
    <div class="container-site">
      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-5">
        <p class="text-lg text-ink-700">
          Most comparison pages are sales sheets with a competitor's name in the title. These are not, and the two rules
          below are what keep them useful.
        </p>
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-ink-200 bg-white p-5">
            <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink-900">No prices, for anyone</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-700">
              Not for Odoo either. Every vendor here prices by region, edition and contract, so a figure published on
              this site would be wrong for most of the people reading it. Where a licensing model differs, we say so
              without numbers. Get a written quote from each and compare the totals, including the implementation.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-ink-200 bg-white p-5">
            <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink-900">Every page says when not to pick Odoo</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-700">
              We sell Odoo work, so a page that concedes nothing would be worth nothing to you. Each comparison names
              the situation where the other product is the right answer, in plain language, and we would rather say it
              here than three months into a project.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-700">
          Where we were not certain of a fact about another vendor's product, it was left out rather than guessed. If
          you find something here that is out of date, tell us and it gets corrected.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {items.length > 0 && (
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container-site">
        <h2 class="h3">Pick the one you are weighing up</h2>
        <div class="mt-8 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
          {items.map((c) => (
            <a href={`/compare/${text(c.slug)}/`} class="card group flex flex-col">
              {text(c.category) && <span class="chip self-start">{text(c.category)}</span>}
              <h3 class="mt-4 text-lg font-semibold">Odoo vs {text(c.product)}</h3>
              {text(c.framing) && <p class="mt-2 flex-1 text-sm text-ink-600">{text(c.framing)}</p>}
              <span class="mt-4 text-sm font-semibold text-brand-600 group-hover:text-brand-700">Read the comparison →</span>
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  )}

  <section class="section pt-0">
    <div class="container-site">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <h2 class="h3">If you are running Odoo already</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700">
          These pages are for choosing a system. If the decision is already made, the work is a rollout or a move off
          the old system, and both have their own pages.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a href="/services/odoo-implementation/" class="btn-secondary">Odoo implementation</a>
          <a href="/services/odoo-migration/" class="btn-secondary">Odoo migration</a>
          <a href="/odoo-community/" class="btn-secondary">Community vs Enterprise</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section bg-ink-50 border-t border-ink-100">
    <div class="container-site text-center">
      <h2 class="h2">Tell us what you are choosing between</h2>
      <p class="lede mx-auto mt-4 max-w-2xl">
        Send the shortlist and what is breaking in the current setup. A 30-minute call is usually enough to say whether
        Odoo belongs on that list, and we will tell you when it does not.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3">
        <a href="/contact/?source=compare" class="btn-primary">Book a 30-minute call</a>
        <a href="/services/odoo-consultancy/" class="btn-secondary">Odoo consultancy</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
